# INVWINPY.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY, run with
# /CFG:PREVY.CFG, a settings file that is not there, on the items of
# TEST/KEYS/PVNOTES.REQ: the preview's loads that the list's selection
# starts, and the row it follows.  DOWN, with the ESC of an A line typed
# as item 2's load starts: the preview says that it did not load.  A
# click gives it the focus, as a key in the list would have the list
# load it again; ENTER there loads it, and ENTER again opens item 2's
# form.  UP stopped the same way, then DOWN: item 2 is read again, as
# the preview showed no item.  DOWN stopped once more, and ENTER in the
# list: item 3's form opens, the preview still saying that it did not
# load.  Item 3, installed in item 1, shows no line of held units, and
# after the lines of its notes that a memo holds what the item form
# says of the rest.  Item 4's notes, a memo's most lines at their
# longest once their TABs are spaces, show whole.  HOME, then SHIFT-F8
# and DOWN: in add mode the focus row is item 2 and the one row chosen
# item 1, which the preview keeps showing; ENTER in the list opens the
# focus row's form, item 2's, and from the preview ENTER opens item 1's
# form, CTRL-E edits it and DEL asks about it.  SPACE chooses item 2 as
# well, and the preview follows the focus row, item 2; SPACE again
# leaves item 1 alone chosen, and the preview shows it.  Before that,
# DEL from the preview asks about the two, and the ENTER of the P line,
# typed with it for the preview, is dropped under the question, which N
# answers.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINPY.SNP is its snapshot; TEST/framchk.py checks
# it.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER
S ITEM1
K DOWN
A ESC
S SSTOP
M 222 DOWN MID
M 222 UP MID
K ENTER
S SLOAD
K ENTER
S SFORM
K ESC ESC UP
A ESC
S SSTOP2
K DOWN
S SBACK
K DOWN
A ESC
K ENTER
S SLIST
K ESC UP
K DOWN
S PART
K DOWN
S FULL
K HOME SHIFT-F8 DOWN
S ADDMODE
K ENTER
S ADDLIST
K ESC
K F6 ENTER
S ADDFORM
K ESC CTRL-E
S ADDEDIT
K ESC DEL
S ADDDEL
K N ESC SPACE
S TWO
K F6 DEL
P ENTER
S TWODEL
K N F6
K SPACE
S ONE
K ALT-F X
